# Synesis Admin (UI + API)

## Mental model

- **Model Registry** (`/models`) maps **pipeline roles** → **provider + model + endpoint**. It does **not** store API keys. In **API overlay** (`overlays/api`), LiteLLM must run with **Prisma** (`DATABASE_URL` + `STORE_MODEL_IN_DB`) so `POST /model/new` works; [`scripts/deploy.sh`](scripts/deploy.sh) patches `litellm-proxy` with the same Postgres URL as admin. Static `litellm-config` entries for `synesis-router` / `synesis-general` / … would otherwise override registry edits.
- **Provider API Keys** (`/settings/providers`) writes **catalog env vars** to the cluster secret (`PUT`/`DELETE` allowlisted to [`provider_catalog.py`](base/admin/app/services/provider_catalog.py)). Same catalog drives both screens.
- **Yarn** (`/yarn/*`): operator views for the **Synesis Yarn** runtime (sessions, events, performance, **Verification**). Admin probes Yarn via `SYNESIS_YARN_URL` (default in-cluster Service on port **8000**). The Yarn **Containerfile** must run the app with **`/opt/app-root/venv/bin/python`** (not bare `python`) so `uvicorn` resolves.
- Prefer links between those pages when copy refers to “configure the key first.”

## Frontend patterns

- **API errors** — use [`apiErrorMessage`](base/admin/frontend/src/api/errorMessage.ts) and [`ApiErrorBanner`](base/admin/frontend/src/components/common/ApiErrorBanner.tsx); reset mutations when closing modals.
- **New routes** — register in [`router.tsx`](base/admin/frontend/src/router.tsx), [`Sidebar.tsx`](base/admin/frontend/src/components/layout/Sidebar.tsx), and extend [`TopBar.tsx`](base/admin/frontend/src/components/layout/TopBar.tsx) breadcrumb labels / `breadcrumbSegmentLabel` for IDs.
- **Styling** — match existing Tailwind + `dark:` usage; reuse `MetricCard`, `EmptyState`, `DataTable` where appropriate.

## Backend

- **FastAPI** — OpenAPI UI at `/api/docs`; schema at `/api/openapi.json`. The SPA catch-all must **not** shadow these (routes registered before `/{full_path:path}`).
- **Consistency** — Prefer shared Pydantic models, `HTTPException(detail=...)`, and tag routers in OpenAPI when touching `main.py`.

